What this license covers, and what the built core contains

The license above covers this repository's own code: the Chimera module in
module/chimera, the scripts in waterbox/ and the documents.

The core package built from it (godot46.chimeraCore) also contains:

- the Godot Engine, built from the submodule extern/godot (4.6.3-stable)
  with the patches in patches/ applied. Godot is under the MIT license
  (extern/godot/LICENSE.txt), copyright Godot Engine contributors, Juan
  Linietsky and Ariel Manzur;
- the third-party libraries Godot keeps in its thirdparty/ folder, each under
  its own license, all listed with their texts in extern/godot/COPYRIGHT.txt;
- Mesa 24.0.9 (MIT), the software OpenGL the core draws with, with the
  patches in waterbox/mesa-patches applied;
- LLVM 18.1.8 (Apache 2.0 with the LLVM exception), which Mesa's llvmpipe
  compiles the shaders with.

Each package carries these texts in its licenses/ folder
(waterbox/package-licenses.json says which). The package carries no game.
